# OG / social preview images

X/Twitter (and Slack/Discord) use different sources depending on the URL:

| URL shared | What sets the card image |
|------------|---------------------------|
| `https://github.com/reagent-systems/teamthink` | **GitHub Social preview** (Settings → Social preview). Not `public/og.png` alone. |
| `https://teamthink.reagent-systems.com` (site) | Next.js `metadata.openGraph` / `twitter` with absolute URLs via `metadataBase`. |

## Site (`teamthink.reagent-systems.com`)

- Keep `public/og.png` at **1200×630**, ideally under **1 MB**.
- Set `metadataBase` to `https://teamthink.reagent-systems.com` in `app/layout.tsx`.
- After deploy, verify page source has absolute `og:image` / `twitter:image`.
- Refresh caches if needed: [Facebook Sharing Debugger](https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug/) (also used by many scrapers).

## GitHub repo card (required for X when linking the repo)

GitHub has **no public API** for social preview upload.

1. Ensure `.github/social-preview.jpg` (or `.png`) exists, **&lt; 1 MB**, ≥ 640×320 (prefer 1280×640).
2. A repo **admin** uploads it once (or when the art changes):

   - Open https://github.com/reagent-systems/teamthink/settings  
   - **Social preview** → **Edit** → **Upload an image…**  
   - Choose `.github/social-preview.jpg`

3. Confirm https://github.com/reagent-systems/teamthink page source `og:image` contains `repository-images` (not `opengraph.githubassets.com`).
4. Optional helper: `scripts/upload-github-social-preview.mjs` (Playwright + saved GitHub login).

After upload, X may cache the old card; re-paste the link or wait for cache expiry.
